\ Regression checks for date-output ownership and structural validity.
\ These are short synthetic tests. They do not need the full sauce.
\ A failed conversion must not leak fields from an earlier answer.

\ Dedicated QA variables have explicit CAL types and cannot be parsed as new types.
The structuretestrank is a wide quantity.
The structurecheckcutletname is a cutlet name assignment.
The structurecheckmonthlength is a month length record.
The structurecheckmonthname is a month name assignment.

To check complete date clearing:
  Put 1 into the complete date status.
  Put 5000 into the complete date answer's year number.
  Put 10 into the complete date answer's cutlet name index.
  Put 503 into the complete date answer's cutlet day.
  Put 20 into the complete date answer's month name index.
  Put 56 into the complete date answer's month day.
  Reset the complete date answer.
  If the complete date status is not 0,
    put "Reset did not invalidate the previous date." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's year number is not 0,
    put "Previous year survived an invalidation." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's cutlet name index is not 0,
    put "Previous cutlet name survived an invalidation." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's cutlet day is not 0,
    put "Previous cutlet day survived an invalidation." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's month name index is not 0,
    put "Previous month name survived an invalidation." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's month day is not 0,
    put "Previous month day survived an invalidation." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date error is blank,
    put "A failed date lacks an explicit error." into the check report; exit.

To check cutlet structure invariants:
  Put 10 into the chosen year's span count.
  Put 3 into the selected cutlet count.
  Put 10 into the cutlet partition's total spans.
  Put 3 into the cutlet partition's part count.
  Put 0 into the cutlet partition's required boundary.
  Put "1" into the structuretestrank.
  Select a cutlet partition from the structuretestrank.
  Verify the selected cutlet partition.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 1,
    put "An ordinary cutlet partition failed the structural audit." into the check report; exit.
  Put 11 into the chosen year's span count.
  Verify the selected cutlet partition.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 0,
    put "An incorrect year span total passed the cutlet audit." into the check report; exit.
  Put 10 into the chosen year's span count.
  Put 4 into the selected cutlet count.
  Verify the selected cutlet partition.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 0,
    put "An incorrect cutlet count passed the audit." into the check report; exit.
  Put 3 into the selected cutlet count.
  Select cutlet names from the structuretestrank.
  Verify the selected cutlet names.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 1,
    put "Valid distinct cutlet names failed the audit." into the check report; exit.
  Put the chosen cutlet names' first into the structurecheckcutletname.
  Put 18 into the structurecheckcutletname's name index.
  Verify the selected cutlet names.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 0,
    put "Out-of-range cutlet name passed the audit." into the check report; exit.
  Put 2 into the structurecheckcutletname's name index.
  Verify the selected cutlet names.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 0,
    put "A repeated cutlet name passed the audit." into the check report; exit.
  Put 1 into the structurecheckcutletname's name index.
  Put 4 into the selected cutlet count.
  Verify the selected cutlet names.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 0,
    put "Wrong number of cutlet names passed the audit." into the check report; exit.

To check month structure invariants:
  Put 128 into the chosen year's year length.
  Put 2 into the selected month count.
  Put "1" into the structuretestrank.
  Select month lengths from the structuretestrank.
  Verify the selected month lengths.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 1,
    put "Valid bounded month lengths failed the audit." into the check report; exit.
  Put 129 into the chosen year's year length.
  Verify the selected month lengths.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 0,
    put "Inexact year length passed the month audit." into the check report; exit.
  Put 128 into the chosen year's year length.
  Put the chosen month lengths' first into the structurecheckmonthlength.
  Put 3 into the structurecheckmonthlength's month length days.
  Verify the selected month lengths.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 0,
    put "Month with fewer than four days passed the audit." into the check report; exit.
  Put 3 into the selected month count.
  Select month names from the structuretestrank.
  Verify the selected month names.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 1,
    put "Valid distinct month names failed the audit." into the check report; exit.
  Put the chosen month names' first into the structurecheckmonthname.
  Put 48 into the structurecheckmonthname's name index.
  Verify the selected month names.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 0,
    put "Out-of-range month name passed the audit." into the check report; exit.
  Put 2 into the structurecheckmonthname's name index.
  Verify the selected month names.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 0,
    put "A repeated month name passed the audit." into the check report; exit.
  Put 1 into the structurecheckmonthname's name index.
  Put 4 into the selected month count.
  Verify the selected month names.
  If the structure audit's passed is not 0,
    put "Wrong number of month names passed the audit." into the check report; exit.
